    <string name="about_summary">Panther VPN for Android</string>
    <string name="about_networks_title">How it connects</string>
    <string name="about_mode_auto_title">Turbo</string>
    <string name="about_mode_auto_body">The fast path. Panther probes a spread of edge addresses on your own network and dials whichever answers best, so a blocked address is routed around rather than retried. The exit stays in your own country by design.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_relay_title">Global</string>
    <string name="about_mode_relay_body">Comes out in another country, which is what geo-restricted services need. It runs inside the Turbo tunnel rather than beside it, so it works on networks where it could not connect on its own. Slower by nature — two hops instead of one. If it cannot come up, Panther keeps you connected on Turbo instead of dropping you.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_stealth_title">Prowl</string>
    <string name="about_mode_stealth_body">The one that keeps going when the others are blocked. It keeps a list of servers, tests them on your own phone and dials whichever actually works, moving to another the moment one stops. On a network that blocks them outright it opens the connection through the Turbo tunnel instead, so the servers stay reachable — the country you come out in is still the server\'s own.</string>
    <string name="about_support_title">Support channel</string>
    <string name="about_credits_title">Built on</string>
    <string name="about_credits_body">Panther bundles open-source components. Every one of them, with its full licence and attribution, is listed in NOTICE.md alongside the source.</string>
